  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>During the qualitative analysis of salt with cation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>, addition of a reagent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Dimethylglyoxime</mi></math>&nbsp;to alkaline solution of the salt gives a bright red precipitate according to the following reaction. So, The reagent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and the cation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mfenced></math> respectively are Dimethylglyoxime and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>dmg</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>Ammonical</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Solution</mi></mrow></mover><munder><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>dmg</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mi>Red</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>colur</mi></mrow></munder><mo>&#8595;</mo></math>,</p>",
